    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0208" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1945v01/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/3–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-22T22:00:00-04:00">March 22, 1945—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>677. The British and Chinese Governments have indicated their general
                        approval<anchor n="3" xml:id="d85-f1"/> of the procedure proposed in the
                    Department’s no. 5.82, March 13, 10 p.m.,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d85-f2"/> with
                    respect to the convening of a committee of jurists at or near Washington prior
                    to the San Francisco <pb facs="0209" n="147" xml:id="pg147"/> Conference. The
                    British Government has suggested that in the event that the Committee should not
                    complete its work prior to the opening of the Conference its deliberation should
                    be continued at San Francisco.</p>
                <p>Please bring this to the attention of the Foreign Office and emphasize the
                    urgency of the matter. In view of the short time remaining before the opening of
                    the Conference, it is essential that invitations be issued soon to enable
                    representatives of governments at a distance from Washington to arrive in time
                    for the meeting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
